English translation of the original Japanese commit message:

ci(release-crates): retry rate limits and document npm release status

Retry cargo publish for the same crate on crates.io HTTP 429 responses,
waiting 660 seconds between attempts, with a limit of 10 attempts.
Other publishing errors still fail immediately. This lets an initial
multi-crate release wait out new-crate rate limits in one workflow run.
Add RELEASING.md with the recorded 0.2.0 registry status: all nine
crates
and the PyPI wheels and sdist were published, while npm was pending.
It documents the reported npm 2FA-token and first-publish OIDC blockers,
workflow retry instructions, and an interactive 2FA publishing option.
